From 8554b8a84d0077cf96875198512af03e774f816a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ARKHE Developer <developer@arkhe.os>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:53:33 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] arkhe: pin Rust 1.96.0, per-package sources, sdd-parser
 and repro checks

- Toolchain from source/rust-toolchain.toml via rust-overlay (locked).
- lib/workspace.nix: each package gets only its path-dependency crate
  closure; other workspace members get empty stub targets.
- New package arkhe-sdd-parser, alias arkhe-verify-cli.
- arkhe-verify checkPhase requires golden_vectors and golden_contract.
- Checks: tests-arkhe-{core,kernel,governance}, tests-clippy (allows the
  pre-existing too_many_arguments and useless_vec lints),
  reproducible-*, source-manifest, toolchain-version, sdd-parser-smoke.
- Snapshot refreshed from the workspace; scripts/update-source.py.
- Track arkhe/lib, which a global `lib/` gitignore had kept out of the
  previous commit.

Observed on x86_64-linux (Nix 2.35.4): nix flake check passes (24 checks);
--rebuild of arkhe-verify, arkhe-verify-wasm and arkhe-sdd-parser is
bit-identical; CA build of arkhe-verify has the same narHash.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
